    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0523" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Reidun/114: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Biddle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-04-15T18:00:00-05:00">April 15, 1936—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Your April 8, 11 a.m. Treaty referred to is presumably liquor treaty signed
                    May 24, 1924. This treaty has no application to <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reidun</hi>
                    <pb facs="0524" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/> case since vessel came voluntarily into
                    our jurisdiction and thereby the ship itself and those on board by their own act
                    became subject to our laws. The seizure of the vessel and the indictment and
                    arrest of the officers were normal result of their previous conduct. The full
                    protection of the law and recourse to our courts is open to them if they wish to
                    avail themselves thereof, and suit to recover vessel instituted at New York.</p>
                <p>See instruction No. 43, March 31, 1936.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d359-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
